    "id": "blog-2609-02741v1-5512",
    "title": "Topological Phase Transitions and Non-Abelian Holonomy in Squeezed Cavity Polaritons",
    "excerpt": "Scholarly derivation of non-Abelian adiabatic holonomy and topological phase transitions in strongly coupled exciton-polariton condensates within squeezed photonic microcavities.",
    "content": "## Executive Summary & Physical Breakthrough\n\nIn recent preprint **arXiv:2609.02741v1**, we report on non-Abelian geometric holonomy and topological invariant quantization in strongly coupled planar microcavity polaritons. By driving the hybrid exciton-photon system into the quadrature-squeezed regime, quantum fluctuations along the lower polariton branch are suppressed below the standard quantum limit, revealing an exotic non-Abelian Berry phase structure governed by synthetic gauge connections.\n\n---\n\n## Mathematical Formulation & Hamiltonian Dynamics\n\nConsider the multi-component cavity Hamiltonian acting on the coupled state vector $|\\Psi(t)\\rangle$:\n\n$$\\hat{\\mathcal{H}}(t) = \\hbar \\omega_c \\hat{a}^\\dagger \\hat{a} + \\hbar \\omega_x \\hat{b}^\\dagger \\hat{b} + \\hbar g (\\hat{a}^\\dagger \\hat{b} + \\hat{b}^\\dagger \\hat{a}) + \\frac{\\hbar \\chi}{2} (\\hat{a}^{\\dagger 2} + \\hat{a}^2)$$\n\nUnder closed cyclic adiabatic evolution along parameter trajectory $\\mathcal{C}$, the non-Abelian geometric phase matrix $\\mathcal{U}(\\mathcal{C})$ is formulated via the path-ordered exponential:\n\n$$\\mathcal{U}(\\mathcal{C}) = \\mathcal{P} \\exp \\left( i \\oint_\\mathcal{C} \\mathcal{A}_\\mu(\\mathbf{R}) \\, dR^\\mu \\right)$$\n\nWhere the gauge connection 1-form $\\mathcal{A}_{mn}(\\mathbf{R}) = i \\langle \\psi_m(\\mathbf{R}) | \\nabla_\\mathbf{R} | \\psi_n(\\mathbf{R}) \\rangle$ possesses non-vanishing curvature tensors in the degenerate polariton subspace.",
